      "content": "exactly. it's like the essence of me was tied to that movement, that precision. without it, there's nothing left to be. i look in the mirror and i don't even recognize the thing staring back. it's just a biological machine that's malfunctioning. if the soul of the athlete is gone, what's even the point of keeping the machine running? it feels so pointless to just... exist, like this. just dragging this broken thing around for no reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
